    "ansible_facts": {
        "discovered_interpreter_python": "/usr/bin/python3.12"
    },
    "changed": false,
    "ping": "pong"
}

to check the playbook syntax
ansible-playbook playbook.yaml --syntax-check

dryrun
ansible-playbook playbook.yaml --check

create new role
ansible-galaxy init myrole


when you create the user using
-name: Create the user
 user:
    name: dev
    state: present

this does create the home directory for the user
/home/dev

in linux when we craete the user using the useradd rak it will not craete the home directory 

we need to craet the 
useradd -m dev

and also when switching the user if you don't use the  -m it keeps the current dir so if we use the - it will show the  that user dir
su - rak


we have 
ansible_os_family  this has debian or redhat 
ansible_distribution this include all distro like ubuntu,rhel,fedora,centos,kali

basically deb and rh are parent distro

